{"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "texalu", "ucas": "it(x: u8 in 0..2, y: u8 in 0..2) = B[y*4 + x] + B[y*4 + x + 1] + B[y*4 + x + 4] + B[y*4 + x + 5]\ntexalu it under cal", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "texalu", "model": "cal", "cost_before": 35.5, "status": "proved", "cost": 33.625, "expr": "int(1020tex_bilinear8([0.0117647061, 0.0352941193, 0.105882354, 0.31764707, 0.952941179, 0.00392156886, 0.784313738, 0.392156869, 0.196078435, 0.0980392173, 0.0470588244, 0.0235294122, 0, 1, 0.501960814, 0.250980407], 4, f32(x) + 1, f32(y) + 1) + 0.5)", "exact": true, "reads": ["4 entries of the 4 x 4 table from offset (0, 0), weights' sum 4: one read at fraction 0.5 along x, 0.5 along y"], "holds_where": "holds where x in [0, 2], y in [0, 2] (proved ranges): every texel read is inside the table", "derivation": ["a linear read at fractions (u, v) of texels a b / c d is (1-u)(1-v) a + u(1-v) b + (1-u)v c + uv d: times 1020 with u = 0.5, v = 0.5 those are the entries' weights (the texels are the entries / 255)", "the fractions are on the 2^-8 grid and the coordinates exact in f32: the weights do not move", "the filter is within 2 ulp of that sum (the model's tex_within): 0.000243; the texels as f32: 3.03e-05; in all 0.000395", "the entries' sum is a whole number and the reads are within 0.000456 of it (with the f32 products and adds): below 1/2, so floor(v + 1/2) is the sum (never negative: the conversion to an integer truncates, which is that floor)", "checked again by evaluation with ucas's own filter (exact weights' sums, one rounding) on all 9 points: equal"], "pipeline": ["a texture R8_UNORM, 4 x 4, one level: the table's entries as bytes (the shader sees k/255)", "a sampler: LINEAR mag and min filters, NEAREST mipmap mode, CLAMP_TO_EDGE, unnormalizedCoordinates, lod 0", "one combined image sampler more in the layout; the shader reads textureLod(s, vec2(x, y), 0.0).r", "setup (the descriptor, the upload) is not in the model: not measured"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "texalu it: reads through the texture unit under cal (cost 35.5 as written):\n  cost 33.625 int(1020tex_bilinear8([0.0117647061, 0.0352941193, 0.105882354, 0.31764707, 0.952941179, 0.00392156886, 0.784313738, 0.392156869, 0.196078435, 0.0980392173, 0.0470588244, 0.0235294122, 0, 1, 0.501960814, 0.250980407], 4, f32(x) + 1, f32(y) + 1) + 0.5)\n      4 entries of the 4 x 4 table from offset (0, 0), weights' sum 4: one read at fraction 0.5 along x, 0.5 along y\n      holds where x in [0, 2], y in [0, 2] (proved ranges): every texel read is inside the table\n      a linear read at fractions (u, v) of texels a b / c d is (1-u)(1-v) a + u(1-v) b + (1-u)v c + uv d: times 1020 with u = 0.5, v = 0.5 those are the entries' weights (the texels are the entries / 255)\n        the fractions are on the 2^-8 grid and the coordinates exact in f32: the weights do not move\n        the filter is within 2 ulp of that sum (the model's tex_within): 0.000243; the texels as f32: 3.03e-05; in all 0.000395\n      the entries' sum is a whole number and the reads are within 0.000456 of it (with the f32 products and adds): below 1/2, so floor(v + 1/2) is the sum (never negative: the conversion to an integer truncates, which is that floor)\n      checked again by evaluation with ucas's own filter (exact weights' sums, one rounding) on all 9 points: equal\n      the pipeline needs (a proposal: nothing is applied):\n        a texture R8_UNORM, 4 x 4, one level: the table's entries as bytes (the shader sees k/255)\n        a sampler: LINEAR mag and min filters, NEAREST mipmap mode, CLAMP_TO_EDGE, unnormalizedCoordinates, lod 0\n        one combined image sampler more in the layout; the shader reads textureLod(s, vec2(x, y), 0.0).r\n        setup (the descriptor, the upload) is not in the model: not measured\n"}
